# Mini App packages: never reformat these.
#
# A built entry document's CSP carries sha256 hashes of its own inline
# <script> and <style> bodies. Reformatting the document changes those bytes
# and the hashes no longer match, so the browser silently refuses to run the
# script or apply the styles — a package that looks fine in a diff and is
# broken at load time. `hello-remote/` is committed with exactly such a CSP,
# and `hello-styled/` is generated by `openmini build`.
#
# This is the same failure mode as Phase 8.5's R1 (hashing bytes that are
# rewritten afterwards), reached from the other direction.
